  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Evaluate $z=\\sqrt{x{y}^{2}-4}$ at the point $(5,-2).$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(5,-2),$ we substitute $x=5$ and $y=-2$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(5,-2)} & =\\sqrt{x{y}^{2}-4}\\,{|}_{(5,-2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5(-2)^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5(4)-4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20-4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
